</style><div class="fluid-engine fe-6874e0b3fecb93179773dab7"><div class="fe-block fe-block-ead6a8b7770b1a91698c"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="ead6a8b7770b1a91698c" id="block-ead6a8b7770b1a91698c"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">My first memory of Charlotte is a city leaving work and very quickly getting in their cars. It was 1991, and I met my uncle at the downtown television station where he worked. At five we stepped into a current of suits flowing out of those mirrored Uptown towers. By the time dinner crossed anyone’s mind, the sidewalks looked as if they had been rolled up and stored for the night.</p><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Three decades later, Charlotte knows what to do after five. Uptown stays busy after dark, while NoDa, Plaza Midwood, Elizabeth, and Dilworth have all developed their own gravitational pull. The best restaurants in <a href="/city-guides/the-south/the-complete-guide-to-charlotte-north-carolina">Charlotte</a> are scattered among them: a six-seat omakase counter, tasting menus built around Radiohead, naturally leavened pizza, and scallop crudo at a neighborhood wine bar.</p><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">The restaurant scene finally feels proportional to the city around it. Charlotte still shows off its ambition in steel and glass. These days, it also serves it for dinner. </p><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">These are the best restaurants in Charlotte right now.<br></p></div>


  
