</div></div></div><div class="fe-block fe-block-447943f87a6a80db7668"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="447943f87a6a80db7668" id="block-447943f87a6a80db7668"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><h3 style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Emmy Lou’s</h3><h4 style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">$$$ | <a target="_blank" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Emmy%20Lou%27s%2C%202400%20Park%20Rd%20Suite%20H%2C%20Charlotte%2C%20NC%2028203">MAP</a> | <a target="_blank" href="https://emmylouswinebar.com/">WEBSITE</a> | <a target="_blank" href="https://www.instagram.com/emmylousclt/">INSTAGRAM</a></h4><p style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Only seven stools line the bar at Emmy Lou’s, with more than 20 wines waiting by the glass and a corner banquette, communal table, and patio for those Piedmont days where there’s nowhere better. Customshop owners Andres Kaifer and Alex Bridges handed the kitchen to former chef Adriana “Dre” Cavazos, <a target="_blank" href="https://emmylouswinebar.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/menu.pdf">whose small plates</a> land with the command of someone who knows how to make dishes sing with few ingredients: pan con tomate with sourdough that’s soaked up garlicky tomatoes; hamachi tiradito with white ponzu and sweet potato causa; and seasonal sundaes that’ll take what’s fresh , like the recent orange and ginger ice cream topped with carrot caramel and pistachio. Sometimes it’s the smallest of places putting out the best of food.</p><p style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true"><strong>Best for:</strong> Wine by the glass with scallop crudo close behind<br></p></div>


  
