  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><h3 style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Mariposa</h3><h4 style="white-space:pre-wrap;">$$$$<span class="sqsrte-text-color--lightAccent">$</span> | <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/mariposa+charlotte/data=!4m2!3m1!1s0x8856a0294e019169:0xb22b0f696e4bb0d4?sa=X&amp;ved=1t:242&amp;ictx=111" target="_blank">MAP</a> | <a href="https://www.mariposaclt.com/" target="_blank">WEBSITE</a> | <a href="https://www.instagram.com/mariposaatthemint/" target="_blank">INSTAGRAM</a></h4><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Mariposa is what happens when a restaurant refuses to be pigeonholed into a single cuisine and instead decides to borrow from everywhere. The menu jumps from chaat-style street snacks to Mediterranean dips to Latin-leaning small plates, yet somehow it all works. The best strategy here is to order generously—maybe the patatas bravas, the coconut curry mussels, and the lamb kefta—and just roll with it.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Best for:</strong> Ordering all over the menu and letting the table sort it out</p><p class="" data-rte-preserve-empty="true" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"></p></div>


  
