</div></div></div><div class="fe-block fe-block-762e5a82132c01aa0129"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/0afe5a90-478c-4ec2-b335-ad74d151c1ea_956/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="762e5a82132c01aa0129" id="block-762e5a82132c01aa0129"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><h3 style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Zamindar’s Clubhouse</h3><h4 style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">$$$$ | <a target="_blank" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Zamindar%27s%20Clubhouse%2C%20155%20New%20Bern%20St%2C%20Charlotte%2C%20NC%2028203">MAP</a> | <a target="_blank" href="https://www.zamindarsclubhouse.com/">WEBSITE</a> | <a target="_blank" href="https://www.instagram.com/zamindars.clubhouse/">INSTAGRAM</a></h4><p style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Sometimes you walk into a restaurant that decidedly feels like somewhere else, and Zamindar’s Clubhouse feels very much transplanted from South Beach. Founder David Pandoria channeled his years working as a Charlotte DJ and built a restaurant that channels nightclub feels. There’s deep green walls, orange banquettes, murals, lots of brass accents, and chandeliers fill the 7,500-square-foot space, with a lounge in the back for those here for more than the curry. Luckily all this flash comes with the food to back it up, thanks to Hyderabad-born chef Vamshi Krishna Adi, whose New York restaurant Ishq earned a Michelin Bib Gourmand. Jalebi chaat pairs chickpea masala with beetroot and crispy sev, ghee-roast scallops get a dusting of gunpowder, and raw mango and coconut sharpen Calicut lobster curry.</p><p style="text-align: start; ; white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true"><strong>Best for:</strong> A dinner that starts with chaat and may end with a dance party<br></p></div>


  
